# Local configuration for NORA Desktop (Tauri + Vite).
# Copy to `.env.local` and adjust. Never commit `.env` with secrets.

# --- API backend ---
# NORA backend URL used in dev by the `npm run dev` script (Vite). In prod the
# Tauri binary uses the value of `plugins.nora.apiBaseUrl` in `tauri.conf.json`,
# or `NORA_API_BASE_URL` baked in at build time by `build.rs`.
NORA_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8080

# ============================================================================
# STT (speech-to-text) — NOTHING TO CONFIGURE HERE, AND THAT IS THE DESIGN
# ============================================================================
# Transcription is the provider's realtime API, reached over a WebSocket with a
# SHORT-LIVED credential that the NORA backend mints per track (ADR 0039/0045).
# Everything that used to be a knob on this side is now a server decision:
#
#   was NORA_STT_BACKEND        -> there is one backend
#   was NORA_WHISPER_MODEL      -> the server picks the model; it pays for it
#   was NORA_WHISPER_MODEL_*    -> there is no model to download or verify
#   was NORA_WHISPER_THREADS    -> there is no local inference
#   was NORA_WHISPER_AUDIO_CTX  -> idem
#   was NORA_WHISPER_FORCE_CPU  -> idem
#
# **DO NOT ADD A PROVIDER API KEY TO THIS FILE.** A key in a distributed desktop
# binary is a published key, and avoiding exactly that is the reason the backend
# mints session credentials at all. To exercise the path locally, point
# NORA_API_BASE_URL at a NORA API that has `NORA_STT_OPENAI_API_KEY` set (see
# `services/api/.env.example`) and log in through the main window — the desktop
# authenticates with the web session cookie, not with a stored token.
